#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "da92ef6c-cb0b-5a4c-9a0d-0f0a9db19616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4403" :question/problem "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f38167e2-3c1d-5c00-9691-ba8e6ac6fdce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices Given the Dimensions of the Factors"}] :question/id #uuid "c677ee1a-d3c2-534c-985c-efaa5dc04c86" :question/math-academy-id "e-4404" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $AB$?" :question/worked-solution "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "9352349d-64e0-5437-9d72-7e7f7e571064" :question/math-academy-id "e-4405" :question/problem "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30f910bd-709e-5567-9db8-b85b93ad6afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282822} {:answer/id #uuid "dc322ef8-3226-57fc-b63c-a80ab088c871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282823} {:answer/id #uuid "f9304ac7-8bb9-54b8-8c7b-7370488ec631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282824} {:answer/id #uuid "435ae3b9-1547-5a37-b2b6-30423833182c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282825} {:answer/id #uuid "1eeee2b3-94cb-5987-a6f8-25979ac2733e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9304ac7-8bb9-54b8-8c7b-7370488ec631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282824} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ae3c67-73ab-5957-bc41-4e7d63059951" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d34ba736-b5e8-5d98-9c72-ef71550ebac1" :question/math-academy-id "q-129437" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $RP$ is well defined\n- The product $SP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f38167e2-3c1d-5c00-9691-ba8e6ac6fdce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices Given the Dimensions of the Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8296355-a8d9-56f3-833a-519ddc4e36b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282829} {:answer/id #uuid "c65d00b6-657f-5855-a50c-237d5a80bba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282830} {:answer/id #uuid "52f679ac-8392-5720-bfca-d699f11b2835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282831} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1baef8-c80f-5f8e-ad0f-e6a9e81e443d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282832} {:answer/id #uuid "bc184f99-1d64-519a-99f7-c8dee07285b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17